  "response_text": "If we didn\u2019t set the PSP using __set_PSP, the processor wouldn\u2019t know where the new thread\u2019s stack is located. When runFirstThread() runs, it expects the process stack (PSP) to point to a valid stack with all the saved register values. Without this setup, the CPU tries to pop values (like PC and xPSR) from an uninitialized or incorrect memory location, leading to invalid instruction execution or memory access \u2014 which causes a hard fault.\\n",
